you can hear the gunshots  echoing through the alleyways as heavily  armed police  pour in an operation on the ground and  on the rooftops  targeting what they say were members of  a drug trafficking gang in one of rio's  biggest favelas  as the police moved in the cameras  captured some of those suspected gang  members trying to escape  jumping from roof to roof some dropping  to the ground  by the time it was all over police said  more than two dozen were dead  among them one of their own officers  among those injured were passengers on a  passing train  who were hit by the crossfire  [Music]  what was the deadliest operation of its  kind in rio's recent history  prompted protests on the same streets  this is wrong they killed my friend this  woman says i want justice  still on the ground the pool of blood  from one of the victims  shell casing scattered around and inside  one of the apartments  a bullet hole in the wall  this woman said police came to her  apartment looking for a gang member  who'd already been shot they came in and  killed the kid in my daughter's room she  said  the police later showed off some of what  they'd seized in the operation  those who survived were arrested but  killings by police are at a record level  this year  brazil's supreme court ruled these  operations should be suspended during  the pandemic  so far this year there have been more  than 250 of them  greg milam sky news
 

